@startuml
title OmniDesk AI Error Handling Workflow

start

:Receive error or failed operation;
:Classify error source and severity;

if (Authentication or authorization error?) then (yes)
  :Reject the request;
  :Return safe authentication or forbidden response;
  :Record safe security event;
elseif (Provider integration error?) then (yes)
  :Identify affected provider and connection;
  :Preserve existing synchronized data;
  :Record classified provider failure;
  :Report provider status to the user;
elseif (Synchronization error?) then (yes)
  :Stop the failed synchronization operation;
  :Preserve previously synchronized data;
  :Record safe diagnostic event;
  :Report synchronization failure;
  :Allow retry where appropriate;
elseif (AI service error?) then (yes)
  :Record AI failure category;
  :Report AI unavailable status;
  :Keep core communication features available;
  :Allow retry where appropriate;
else (unknown or unexpected error)
  :Record safe diagnostic event;
  :Return a generic error response;
  :Avoid exposing internal details;
endif

:Monitor and reassess the failure;
stop

note right
Error logs must not contain passwords,
tokens, session secrets, or unnecessary
communication content.
end note

@enduml
